// icon.rc
//
// Deliberately no "#define IDI_ICON1 101" here: the RC compiler's preprocessor would substitute
// IDI_ICON1 -> 101 in the line below, embedding the icon under the NUMERIC resource ID 101. But
// wxICON(IDI_ICON1) (used in LauncherWindow.cpp/ProgressWindow.cpp) stringifies its argument and
// looks the icon up by NAME ("IDI_ICON1") at runtime via LoadIcon - a name/ID mismatch that fails
// with ERROR_RESOURCE_TYPE_NOT_FOUND (0x715), even though the RC compile step itself succeeds.
// Leaving IDI_ICON1 undefined keeps it a literal resource name, matching the name-based lookup.
IDI_ICON1 ICON "icon.ico"
